# Impact analysis

Playbook rule: schema / API / shared-interface changes get a blast-radius analysis and an approved plan before any edit.

## Triggers

Run an impact analysis before changing any of:

- API contracts or DTOs (`data/remote/api/`, `data/remote/dto/`).
- `ApiResult`, `AppError`, `UiText`, `LoadState`, `UiEffect` or `BaseViewModel`.
- Design tokens (`core/designsystem/theme/`).
- Public parameters of shared components in `core/designsystem` or `core/ui`.
- Gradle flavors, `config/env/*.properties` or the version catalog (`gradle/libs.versions.toml`).
- The Android manifest.

## Procedure

- Run the `impact-analysis` skill.
- Write `../resturant-app-architecture/docs/06-development/impact-analyses/IA-YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md` from `../resturant-app-architecture/templates/IMPACT-ANALYSIS-template.md`.
- List the consumers found by search together with the exact commands used (for example `rg -n "LoadState" app/src`).
- State the risk level (Low / Medium / High) and why.
- Order the plan as `API → clients → tests → docs`.
- Include rollback steps.
- Stop and wait for human approval before editing any file the analysis covers.
- Implement only what the approved analysis covers; if scope grows, update the analysis and ask again.
